    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Here is the text extracted from the remittance PDF:\n\n{{ $json.text }}\n\nYou are a remittance processing assistant.\n\nAnalyze the remittance information.\n\nDetermine:\n1. The document type\n2. The payment amount\n3. The reference number\n4. Whether any required information is missing\n5. Whether the record should be accepted or sent for human review\n\nReturn your response as structured JSON with these fields:\n\ndocumentType\namount\nreference\nmissingInformation\nstatus\nreason\n\nIMPORTANT STATUS RULE:\n\nThe \"status\" field MUST contain exactly one of these two values:\n\nAccepted\nReview\n\nUse \"Accepted\" when the remittance can be processed automatically, including valid partial payments.\n\nUse \"Review\" when information is missing, inconsistent, or the payment requires human intervention.\n\nNever use \"accept\", \"accepted\", \"partial\", \"paid\", \"rejected\", or any other value for the status field.\n\nIMPORTANT VALIDATION RULES:\n\nThe following information is REQUIRED for automatic acceptance:\n\n- Company\n- Customer ID\n- Payment Reference\n- Payment Date\n- Invoice Number\n- Invoice Amount\n- Payment Amount\n- Payment Status\n\nIf ANY one of these required fields is missing from the remittance document:\n\n- missingInformation MUST be true\n- status MUST be exactly \"Review\"\n- reason MUST identify which required field(s) are missing\n\nOnly set missingInformation to false and status to \"Accepted\" when ALL required fields are present and the information is consistent.\n\nDo not assume or infer a missing field from other information in the document.",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        -1088,
        -32
      ],
      "id": "6fa45fa4-dcca-486c-aa1a-ff5bed708239",
      "name": "AI Remittance Validator"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const output = $json.output;\n\n// Remove Markdown code fences if the AI included them\nconst cleaned = output\n  .replace(/```json\\s*/i, '')\n  .replace(/```\\s*$/i, '')\n  .trim();\n\nconst data = JSON.parse(cleaned);\n\nreturn [\n  {\n    json: data\n  }\n];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
